# Pen over a flat colour wash.
#
# Two passes over the same photograph. Underneath, the colour is flattened and
# reduced to a handful of tones so it reads as something laid in with a brush.
# Over it, the picture again as line work, multiplied so the white paper of the
# line layer disappears and only the lines remain.
#
# `weight` is where the line layer's white point sits, inverted so that larger
# means heavier. It is the parameter that decides what the result *is*: edge
# detection returns a continuous field, not lines, and the white point is what
# turns that field into marks by throwing away everything faint. Set it high
# and every leaf edge and every crack in the stone becomes a stroke, which
# reads as scribble rather than as drawing.

param ink = 0.8
param wash = 5
param weight = 0.42

filter median radius={min*0.006}
filter surface-blur radius={min*0.022} threshold=0.22
adjust posterize levels={wash}
adjust hue-saturation saturation=-0.08
adjust levels out-black=0.05 out-white=0.99

place
adjust black-and-white
filter find-edges
adjust levels black=0.06 white={1-weight}
set name="Ink" blend="Multiply" opacity={ink}
layer flatten
